# Astro Inline Editor

Dev-only editor. Copy lives in JSON; layout stays in Astro. Fields are opt-in — no route registry.

## Architecture

- **JSON content** → `src/data/**/*.json` (or subfolders you choose)
- **Layout** → `.astro` templates (icons, images, links, structure)
- **Editable fields** → `contentEdit(file, path)` or `contentEdit(file, path, true)` for HTML
- **Dev toolbar** → open "Inline Editor" in Astro's dev toolbar to Edit / Save / Cancel
- **Static HTML** → any `.html` under `public/` is fully editable (text leaves only)

## New page checklist

When creating an editable page:

1. Create JSON: `src/data/<area>/<slug>.json` with `meta`, `hero`, sections, etc.
2. Create/refactor `.astro` to `import content from "..."` and render layout
3. Define `const CONTENT_FILE = "src/data/.../file.json"`
4. Import `contentEdit` from `astro-inline-editor` (or `astro-inline-editor/content-edit`)
5. Helper: `const edit = (p, html) => contentEdit(CONTENT_FILE, p, html)`
6. Wire every editable string: `{...edit("hero.title")}` on the element
7. HTML with links/bold: `{...edit("path", true)}` + `set:html={value}`
8. Hero title: pass `titleEditFile` + `titleEditPath` to `PageHeader` if supported
9. Section H2s: store `heading` in JSON; derive QuickNav labels from headings
10. Lists/stats: text in JSON arrays; icons/themes stay in Astro by index

## Do NOT

- Put layout, icons, image paths, or link URLs in JSON unless they are content (e.g. CTA label + href as content)
- Rely on route allowlists — pages are editable when tagged, not when listed in config
- Edit `.astro` source for copy on JSON-backed pages
- Expect dynamic `[slug]` routes to work without explicit JSON path wiring

## HTML vs plain text

- Plain text field → `edit("sections.intro")` with `{value}` children
- HTML field (links, `<strong>`) → `edit("sections.intro", true)` with `set:html={value}`

## Example wiring

```astro
---
import content from "../../data/pages/about.json";
import { contentEdit } from "astro-inline-editor";

const FILE = "src/data/pages/about.json";
const edit = (path, html = false) => contentEdit(FILE, path, html);
---

<h1 {...edit("hero.title")}>{content.hero.title}</h1>
<p {...edit("hero.intro", true)} set:html={content.hero.intro} />
```

## Config (astro.config)

```js
import inlineEditor from "astro-inline-editor";

export default defineConfig({
  integrations: [
    inlineEditor({
      excludeRoots: ["/admin"], // optional blocklist only
    }),
  ],
});
```
